# Every image except infra/ota builds from the repository root
# (infra/compose/docker-compose.yml): apps/web needs the root package-lock.json
# for the @ada/shared workspace, and the Python services install
# libs/python/ada-core and libs/python/ada-platform from source. Docker reads
# only the .dockerignore at the root of the context, so this one file covers
# all of them. Each Dockerfile then COPYs only what it needs, so anything listed
# here is unreachable from a Dockerfile by construction.
.git
.venv
**/.venv/
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache/
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.expo
**/.vite
**/.turbo
data
docs
infra
scripts
Makefile
*.pdf

# apps/field/ is in the npm workspace, so its manifest has to be in the context
# for `npm ci` to validate the lockfile — none of its source is built here.
apps/field/*
!apps/field/package.json

apps/keycloak-theme

# Python build and test artefacts
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Test suites. The images run no tests; shipping them only invalidates layers.
**/tests/

# Training code and configs — a research tree, not part of the serving image.
services/ml-worker/training/

# Secrets. .env is gitignored, but a build context is not a git checkout, and
# an .env copied into a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Documentation and editor state — no image needs them, and they invalidate the
# build cache on every edit.
**/*.md
!**/README.md
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
